WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:04.133
In previous videos, you could see us renovating an old pickup.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:07.015
We also got a new container, and installed a big roof on it.

00:00:07.015 --> 00:00:10.897
Our workspace team is now getting into a new fascinating project!

00:00:10.897 --> 00:00:12.494
Remember the yellow van?

00:00:12.494 --> 00:00:14.683
It's been here since Season 1!

00:00:14.683 --> 00:00:18.472
In this video, we are going to renovate it, 
 and make it into a long-term living space.

00:00:18.472 --> 00:00:20.720
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update!

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.557
This old German post-office van
 was one of the first additions to Basekamp!

00:00:29.557 --> 00:00:32.290
It was donated by our friend Mattia during Season 1.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:36.920
But, after two years,  its state is a bit - let's say - rough...

00:00:41.678 --> 00:00:47.018
Yeah, the van is rusting, and falling kind of apart...

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.790
It has some leaks...

00:00:55.946 --> 00:00:57.745
Problems with the electricity...

00:00:57.745 --> 00:01:01.020
It's not insulated, and it is not fully leveled...

00:01:02.356 --> 00:01:08.757
So, this year we decided to give it a bit more care,
to make it more useful, and more comfy, for the people that come.

00:01:08.757 --> 00:01:12.283
The van, originally, was designed to be a campervan.

00:01:12.283 --> 00:01:15.753
But, realistically, this is not going to drive much more...

00:01:15.753 --> 00:01:17.752
So, we want to adapt it to our new setup.

00:01:18.068 --> 00:01:21.768
We want to redistribute all the furniture that is in the van.

00:01:21.768 --> 00:01:26.839
And, with that, we want to reuse as much materials
 as we can, from the old setup.

00:01:26.839 --> 00:01:29.208
All of this means a lot of work for us!

00:01:29.208 --> 00:01:33.401
But, in another case, the van would end up in a scrapyard,
 and we don't like that...

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.351
So, for us, it's worth to take the challenge,
and effort, to make it happen!

00:01:37.825 --> 00:01:41.802
Luckily, we come with the help of Jaime, Mariona, and Kevin.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.912
You already know Jaime, but let me introduce you to Kevin and Mariona!

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.065
Hey there! I'm Mariona!

00:01:49.065 --> 00:01:53.016
I'm 26 years old, and I come from a little town, close to Barcelona.

00:01:53.522 --> 00:01:57.233
I'm a product designer, and have worked on it for some years now.

00:01:57.233 --> 00:02:01.855
I came to Project Kamp, because I believe in 
a more sustainable way of life and work.

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:04.161
All of this, and surrounded by nature!

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:08.833
I love the sea, dancing under the rain, and swimming in waterfalls.

00:02:09.842 --> 00:02:16.074
I also like sewing, repairing clothes, and I am interested in how 
to produce new materials out of organic waste.

00:02:16.074 --> 00:02:19.491
Believe it, or not, but we can create material from this orange peel!

00:02:20.503 --> 00:02:23.180
To be honest, the future is kind of blurry for me...

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:26.716
I go step by step, figuring out of what comes next.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.920
But, for sure, I am learning along the way,
 from the amazing people I meet!

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.690
Hello! My name is Kevin!

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:39.524
I'm 36 years old, and I come from Hong Kong!

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:45.053
I'm an upcycling designer, and my focus is on creating
 new objects with waste material.

00:02:45.243 --> 00:02:49.079
I like bringing surprises to people, with materials that are often overlooked.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:55.626
Now, I'm at Project Kamp, because I believe there's a way
 we can live without harming the environment.

00:02:56.638 --> 00:03:01.370
In the future, I would like to bring the inspiration I found here,
back to the society where I came from.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:06.228
But, now, I'm quite excited to be here,
and help the project with my skills!

00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:07.871
See ya!

00:03:09.041 --> 00:03:12.365
Okay, so, the first thing for this project,
 is going to be levelling the van.

00:03:12.365 --> 00:03:15.962
The van has been standing on old tires, 
and they keep losing air...

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.269
So, it's going out of level...

00:03:18.945 --> 00:03:25.315
So, the first thing is to put the van on wooden blocks, 
and getting it level to start building.

00:03:25.631 --> 00:03:29.080
The first thing we do is cutting the stone into four pieces.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.332
Wow!

00:05:12.332 --> 00:05:14.332
Done - it's done!

00:05:50.295 --> 00:05:51.757
That was the last one?

00:05:51.757 --> 00:05:53.295
- Yes! Done, done!

00:05:53.295 --> 00:05:54.174
Nice!

00:05:57.948 --> 00:05:59.346
We just finished leveling the van!

00:05:59.346 --> 00:06:02.622
And, as you can see, all four wheels are floating in the air right now!

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:05.496
So, it doesn't matter if they have no pressure.

00:06:05.496 --> 00:06:09.987
They are now standing on four big wood beams.

00:06:09.987 --> 00:06:13.513
And, it's, it's totally levelled!

00:06:13.513 --> 00:06:16.129
So, now, it's time for the fun part!

00:06:16.129 --> 00:06:17.915
Let's go rip everything out!

00:06:35.527 --> 00:06:37.581
An emergency box, someone?

00:07:35.795 --> 00:07:38.732
- Give me that 
 - Give me that

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:59.818
There's another frame underneath!

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:44.741
So, here we are!

00:11:44.741 --> 00:11:47.633
We have everything from the van sorted!

00:11:47.949 --> 00:11:49.931
Wood from the floor, wood from the walls...

00:11:50.405 --> 00:11:53.979
We will try to reuse everything,
 and that's why they are all sorted so tidally.

00:11:54.232 --> 00:11:57.095
A lot of Styrofoam, which we have no idea what to do with...

00:11:57.095 --> 00:12:00.312
So, I guess, a lot of research needs to be done.

00:12:01.387 --> 00:12:03.231
- Looks good eh?

00:12:05.065 --> 00:12:06.216
It's empty!

00:12:09.108 --> 00:12:10.310
It's not that bad...

00:12:12.428 --> 00:12:13.430
It could be worse.

00:12:13.841 --> 00:12:15.960
I was expecting it worse, actually...

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.121
Nests.

00:12:18.121 --> 00:12:19.317
And, it's full of wasps, yeah?

00:12:19.475 --> 00:12:21.366
- Uh, I don't think so...

00:12:21.366 --> 00:12:22.372
- At least one...

00:12:22.562 --> 00:12:24.010
I see two already!

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:26.010
- There are six! There were six!

00:12:30.501 --> 00:12:33.373
Now you fit, fully! Did you fit before?

00:12:33.373 --> 00:12:34.748
- This is the same roof, huh?

00:12:35.244 --> 00:12:36.803
- But the floor.

00:12:36.803 --> 00:12:40.966
- But the floor was like this, about five centimeters...

00:12:40.966 --> 00:12:42.979
I have a little bit more.

00:12:44.263 --> 00:12:46.491
So, we already took everything apart...

00:12:46.491 --> 00:12:50.931
We ripped everything out, and the last thing is to take the solar system out...

00:12:50.931 --> 00:12:53.701
- I'm taking the wires out...

00:13:04.057 --> 00:13:05.023
Not for now...

00:13:09.086 --> 00:13:10.140
It's stuck somewhere...

00:13:19.058 --> 00:13:20.937
And now, where is it going to?

00:14:03.381 --> 00:14:07.665
It's coming up!... Yay!

00:14:10.987 --> 00:14:12.262
Another one!

00:15:19.231 --> 00:15:23.910
So, okay, I've been trying to take 
this metal wall out, with this tiny grinder...

00:15:24.669 --> 00:15:29.739
It's not working at all, so, it's time for the big one!

00:16:14.813 --> 00:16:16.160
Not enough...

00:16:22.909 --> 00:16:24.177
No way...

00:16:52.967 --> 00:16:54.325
Want a sock?

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:57.240
It's nice...

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:02.734
So, now, we are gonna measure the inside of the van.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:07.755
We're gonna have a top view drawing,
 and then we can decide where to put everything.

00:17:08.008 --> 00:17:10.213
The distribution of the new house!

00:17:11.173 --> 00:17:13.089
And, yeah, that's what we're going to do now!

00:17:13.848 --> 00:17:15.304
- Like, from there...

00:17:15.304 --> 00:17:16.474
Yeah, exactly! 

00:17:37.502 --> 00:17:40.696
Now, that we have all the measurements,
 we will start designing the layout.

00:17:41.328 --> 00:17:45.711
It will take some days to figure out 
the best distribution for our interior...

00:17:50.821 --> 00:17:54.131
Anyway, it seems like the three of us have a similar idea.

00:17:54.131 --> 00:17:55.873
Cool! Let's see how it goes!

00:17:55.873 --> 00:17:57.133
- We have the same layout!

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:05.360
Okay, so, now that the van is cleaned, and everything 
 is ripped apart, we want to bring power to the van.

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:09.307
So, we're gonna dig a trench,
all the way from the pizza hut to the van.

00:18:09.307 --> 00:18:10.680
So, that the van has power...

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:08.265
Oh my God...

00:19:08.265 --> 00:19:08.925
- Almost?

00:19:08.925 --> 00:19:09.896
- Here...

00:19:13.449 --> 00:19:14.252
Yes!

00:19:14.252 --> 00:19:17.771
- Woo!

00:19:17.771 --> 00:19:18.587
We got it!

00:19:18.587 --> 00:19:19.449
- It's out...

00:19:21.152 --> 00:19:22.780
- A little bit more

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:23.699
That's it.

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:50.973
Okay, so, this door doesn't open from the outside...

00:19:50.973 --> 00:19:55.524
So, we were thinking about fixing it, but it's too complicated....

00:19:55.524 --> 00:19:58.194
And, we also found this old door!

00:19:58.194 --> 00:20:01.416
So, we're gonna try fit this door in this opening.

00:20:01.416 --> 00:20:06.869
Our next step is to build a frame
for the door, and try to fit the door in the opening.

00:22:58.920 --> 00:23:03.693
So, we want to use this door for the van,
 and put it in the frame we just made.

00:23:03.693 --> 00:23:06.675
Before we can do that, we have to cut it to size.

00:23:07.118 --> 00:23:09.535
We also have to turn around the hinges...

00:23:09.535 --> 00:23:13.720
And, because we're turning around the hinges, 
we have to turn around the lock.

00:23:41.160 --> 00:23:43.666
So, I wanted to reuse the lock from the door.

00:23:43.666 --> 00:23:46.338
I tried to turn it around, but I broke it...

00:23:47.264 --> 00:23:48.703
Sometimes this happens...

00:23:49.146 --> 00:23:52.805
I'll tell Adrian to get another one, and we will install it later.

00:23:52.805 --> 00:23:55.760
So, meanwhile, let's continue with the door.

00:25:27.902 --> 00:25:31.135
Woah, I don't recognise it!

00:25:39.741 --> 00:25:42.915
Okay, so, right now, we are on the roof of the yellow van.

00:25:43.927 --> 00:25:46.279
As you can see, the fiberglass is looking pretty bad...

00:25:46.279 --> 00:25:51.620
It's bended, it's leaking everywhere, and it's falling apart.

00:25:52.189 --> 00:25:58.418
It has been fixed a few times,
 but the fixes are not the best, as you can see...

00:25:58.418 --> 00:26:04.109
So, we have to take a drastic decision,
 and we have to cut all of the roof out.

00:26:18.399 --> 00:26:23.027
Yeah, so, we are wearing a lot of protection,
because we are going to cut the fiberglass on the roof.

00:26:23.027 --> 00:26:26.653
And, once we cut the fiber, it will be flying all around...

00:26:26.653 --> 00:26:30.530
That's why we are having extra protection!

00:26:30.530 --> 00:26:32.151
- A mask...

00:26:34.860 --> 00:26:36.285
- And, some glasses.

00:27:44.440 --> 00:27:45.631
How are you, guys?

00:27:46.548 --> 00:27:47.685
- I want to take this off!

00:27:47.875 --> 00:27:48.711
Yeah...

00:27:49.565 --> 00:27:50.837
- It's so hot!

00:27:50.837 --> 00:27:52.320
I'm dripping already!

00:27:52.320 --> 00:27:55.758
The dust isn't as bad as we described it...

00:27:56.244 --> 00:27:57.615
- The dust is okay.

00:27:57.615 --> 00:27:59.579
- Yeah, it's not that bad.

00:27:59.579 --> 00:28:05.985
-  But still, I prefer wearing all this stuff,
 because if you get fiberglass on your skin...

00:28:06.839 --> 00:28:10.339
- You're gonna be regretting it for two weeks.

00:28:13.058 --> 00:28:15.789
- It sounds like I want to try a bit. 
 - Yeah?

00:28:16.105 --> 00:28:17.369
- Never try!

00:28:17.369 --> 00:28:19.160
- Go for it...

00:30:19.640 --> 00:30:20.850
Are you okay?

00:30:20.850 --> 00:30:22.249
- I'm okay, I'm okay!

00:30:43.025 --> 00:30:45.243
- Hi Jaime! Say hi!

00:30:45.243 --> 00:30:46.783
Hello!

00:30:46.783 --> 00:30:47.970
- How is it?

00:30:47.970 --> 00:30:50.608
Hot! Very hot!

00:30:51.967 --> 00:30:54.224
But, it worked!

00:30:54.224 --> 00:30:55.458
It's done!

00:30:55.679 --> 00:30:56.909
Better than we thought.

00:30:57.257 --> 00:30:58.966
Easier than we thought.

00:30:59.630 --> 00:31:00.775
New house!

00:31:00.775 --> 00:31:02.412
- Yeah, I like the new roof!

00:31:02.412 --> 00:31:05.749
- Much more open, sunlight, natural light is good!

00:31:05.749 --> 00:31:08.571
- Yeah, that's how we keep it!

00:31:12.993 --> 00:31:14.470
Oof, that was wild!

00:31:15.798 --> 00:31:18.876
Now, we have a completely empty campervan!

00:31:18.876 --> 00:31:22.369
We still don't know what we will do with the old roof, but let's see!

00:31:23.223 --> 00:31:24.601
For now, we are done with this update.

00:31:24.601 --> 00:31:28.814
In the next video, we will finish the van, 
with the new roof, the interior, and details!

00:31:29.193 --> 00:31:32.482
If you want to watch it now, and without ads, 
you can support us on Patreon!

00:31:33.019 --> 00:31:36.032
If not, you can subscribe, and help us with the algorithm.

00:31:36.032 --> 00:31:38.100
Thanks for watching, and see you in the next update!

